course: dictionary
lesson: 2313
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Crop can name a plant that farmers grow, or it can be an action word meaning to cut something off. «Rice, wheat and maize are the most important crops in the world.» Here a crop is a plant.
explain: The words around it are the clues. Words like farmers, soil, grow and harvest point to the plant meaning. Words like photo, picture and hair point to the cutting meaning. «Cropping a photo can make a crowd look small or huge.» Cropping is something you do to a photo, so the cutting meaning fits.
explain: Always test your meaning in the sentence. In «Bees pollinate many fruit crops», swapping in cut off makes no sense, so crop means a plant here. Ask yourself: does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: A crop is a plant grown in large amounts by farmers, like wheat, rice, potatoes or apples.
fact: «Bees pollinate many fruit crops, such as apples and strawberries.» Pollinate means carrying pollen so a plant can make fruit.
fact: A crop can also mean the amount of plant gathered in one season, as in «We had a good crop this year.»
fact: To crop a picture is to cut off the edges you do not want. To crop hair is to cut it very short.
fact: «Crop up» means to appear suddenly, like a problem that crops up when you least expect it.
exercise: «Rice, wheat and maize are the most important crops in the world.» What is a crop in this sentence? | *A plant grown by farmers | A bag for carrying food | A picture with its edges cut off | A short haircut
exercise: «Cropping a photo can make a crowd look small or huge.» What does cropping mean here? | *Cutting off the edges you do not want | Taking a photo with a bright flash | Growing plants in a field | Cutting hair very short
exercise: A farmer says, «We had a good crop this year.» Ella thinks crop means a haircut. What is the best answer? | *Ella is wrong, here crop means the amount of plant gathered in one season | A crop is a kind of bee | A crop is a type of soil | Ella is right, it always means a haircut
test: What does crop mean in «She decided to crop her hair short for the summer»? | A plant with pollen | To grow in a field | *To cut very short | A harvest of fruit
test: In «Egypt is mostly desert, but the Nile left rich black mud along its banks, perfect for crops», which word is the best clue that crops grow in soil? | desert | Egypt | summer | *mud
exam: What does crop mean in «Egypt is mostly desert, but the Nile left rich black mud along its banks, perfect for crops»? | *A plant grown by farmers | A bag for carrying seeds | To cut off the edges | To cut hair very short
